G      CodingH

        The scale application will : 

                o    Be Called "SCALE.COM"
                o    Be written in 'C'.
                o    Not exceed 30K of object code.
                o    Run as a task under MOS 4.10.
                o    Run under DOS 3.0 - 5.0.
                o    Read the tariff/mail class data file during 
                     initialisation.
                o    Not access the floppy disk after initialisation.
                o    Show the software version and referance data issue
                     numbers on screen.


        The tariff/mail class data file will:

                o    Be Called "MAILCLAS.DAT"
                o    Contain an issue number between 000 and 999.
                o    Contain all mail class information.
                o    Contain all tariff information.
                o    Contain all additional service information.
                o    Be less than 5K in size.
                o    Be encripted for security reasons.
                o    Be generated by a seperate utility called
                     CONFSCAL.EXE.

         NOTE : The MAILCLAS.DAT supplied will conform to the mail
                class/tariff information for Sept. 1991 and will be
                coded as issue 000.

        The scale configuration utility will : 

                o    Be Called "CONFSCAL.EXE".
                o    Be written in 'C'.
                o    Run under MOS 4.10.
                o    Run under DOS 3.0 - 5.0.
                o    Read/Write the tariff/mail class input data file.
                o    Create the MAILCLAS.DAT data file.
                o    Allow modification of the tariff information.
                o    Allow modification of the mail class information.
                o    Allow modification of the additional services
                     information.


G      DesignH

        The Application will be designed using SSADM and will consist
        of:

                MAILCLAS.DAT

                    Entity Relationship Diagram

                SCALE.COM

                    Context level Data Flow Diagram
                    Program Structure Diagram
                    Typical Invocation Dialogue Structure
                    Entity Relationship Diagram (as MAILCLAS.DAT)
                    Scale interface/protocol specification
                    Suggested ECCO+ interface specification

                CONFSCAL.EXE

                    Entity Relationship Diagram (input data file)
                    Context level Data Flow Diagram
                    Program Structure Diagram


G      DocumentationH

        In addition to the SSADM design the following documentation
        will be provided for SCALE.COM and CONFSCAL.EXE:

                o    Instalation guide and System overview.
                o    User Operations manual.

G      OperationH

        The scale application "SCALE.COM"

        1.  SCALE.COM will be started as a task via the AUTOEXEC.BAT 
            file at start of day.

        2.  Each time a scale operation is required the ECCO+ application 
            will PAM switch to the scale task.

        3.  The scale application will then handle all input/output from/to 
            the keyboard, screen and scale.  After the operator has selected 
            the required mail class and additional services,  all the 
            information regarding the transaction will be placed in a
            RAM disk file or a pipe.
        
        4.  SCALE.COM will PAM switch back to task 0 (the ECCO+ task).  

        5.  SCALE.COM will then wait until it is selected again.

        NOTE: under DOS,  PAM switching will not occur and the software
              will run continuiously through step 3.

        The data passed to the ECCO+ application will contain the following 
        information:

                Transaction Error Status. i.e. (OK, ERROR, VOIDED)
                Weight.
                Mail Class and price.
                Each additional service and price.
                Total price.
                Checksum.

        The Scale Configuration utility "CONFSCAL.EXE"

        1.  CONFSCAL.EXE will accept input from an input data file
            specified as a command line argument and will then display 
            all the mail class information and relavant additional services.

        3.  The operator will then be able to Insert/Delete/Modify
            each mail class description and their sub menu's.
            Add/Delete which additional services are releted to
            that mail class.
        
        4.  Upon pressing F1, all the tariff information for the
            selected mail class will be displayed and may be
            adjusted.

        5.  Upon pressing F2, all additional services and their
            pricing information will be displayed and may be
            adjusted.

        6.  Upon pressing F3, the output data file MAILCLAS.DAT will
            be generated along with a report file outlineing the
            current data file and the input data file will be written
            to a new file specified as a command line argument.

        7.  Upon pressing F4, the application will enter a symulation
            mode for testing the integrity of the output data file.

        8.  If at any time ESCAPE is pressed the application will ask
            for conformation that the operator wishes to exit the
            program.  If any modifation has occured the program will
            ask for conformation the data changes should not be saved.

